IMPORT prelude

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 (Commonwealth of Australia) -- superannuation: the spouse contribution tax offset (ss 290-230,
-- 290-235), the non-concessional contributions cap (ss 291-20(2), 292-85(2)), downsizer contributions (s 292-102), the transfer
-- balance cap (ss 294-30, 294-35), member benefits at 60 (ss 301-10, 301-15) and death benefits (ss 302-60, 302-140, 302-145,
-- 302-195).
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 267, compilation date 27 August 2026 (includes amendments up to Act No. 79, 2026; register id
-- C2026C00400, 12 volumes), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2004A05138.txt.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0001 in subjects/au/requirements.jsonl (priority 1): raised 24 times by the three Western
-- Australian cradle-to-grave lives. This module answers chloe c057 (a spouse contribution, 2030), jake k089 ($100,000 as a
-- non-concessional contribution at 54, 2060), chloe c094 (downsizer contributions after selling Baldivis, 2070), chloe c092 and
-- daniel d083 (pensions after 60; the transfer balance cap), and the death benefits in chloe c087, c096, c098, jake k098 and
-- daniel d093. SCOPED to those questions.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Indexation (Subdiv 960-M, s 960-285): the concessional contributions cap and the general transfer balance cap
-- for any year after 2017-18 are INPUTS, as is anyone's total superannuation balance; the bring-forward of the non-concessional
-- cap (s 292-85(3)-(8)); the work test and age limits that live in the SIS Regulations (not retrieved); transfer balance credits
-- and debits (Subdivs 294-B, 294-C) and proportional indexation (s 294-40); elements untaxed in the fund (Subdiv 301-C, s 302-85,
-- 302-90), the low rate cap (s 301-20), income streams to dependants under 60 (ss 302-70, 302-75), defined benefit income
-- (Div 303); the tax free and taxable components themselves (Subdiv 307-C); interdependency (s 302-200) beyond one input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR PUBLIC USE. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1997 -- superannuation`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lesser of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `290-230, 290-235 -- spouse contribution tax offset`

-- s 290-230(2): only if the person was your spouse, both were Australian residents when you contributed, "(c) the total of your
-- spouse's: (i) assessable income ...; and (ii) *reportable fringe benefits total; and (iii) *reportable employer superannuation
-- contributions; for the income year is less than $40,000"; (3) not if "living separately and apart ... on a permanent basis";
-- (4A) not if the spouse exceeded the non-concessional cap or had a total superannuation balance at or above the general
-- transfer balance cap (collapsed to one input).
-- s 290-235(1): the offsets "cannot exceed 18% of the lesser of the following: (a) $3,000 reduced by the amount (if any) by
-- which the total mentioned in paragraph 290-230(2)(c) for the income year exceeds $37,000; (b) the sum of the *spouse
-- contributions you make in the income year." (2) "The maximum *tax offset ... is $540".
GIVEN `spouse income total` IS A NUMBER, `spouse contributions` IS A NUMBER, `both resident and living together` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `spouse over a cap` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse contribution offset` MEANS
    IF `both resident and living together` AND (NOT `spouse over a cap`) AND `spouse income total` LESS THAN 40000
    THEN `the lesser of` 540 (`the lesser of` (3000 MINUS (`the greater of` (`spouse income total` MINUS 37000) 0)) `spouse contributions` TIMES 18 DIVIDED BY 100)
    ELSE 0

§§ `291-20(2), 292-85(2) -- non-concessional contributions cap`

-- s 291-20(2): the concessional contributions cap is "(a) for the 2017-2018 financial year -- $25,000; or (b) for the 2018-2019
-- financial year or a later financial year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually" (an INPUT; the note says "annual
-- indexation does not necessarily increase the amount of the cap: see section 960-285").
-- s 292-85(2): the non-concessional contributions cap is "(a) ... 4 times your *concessional contributions cap under subsection
-- 291-20(2) for the year; or (b) if, immediately before the start of the year, your *total superannuation balance equals or
-- exceeds the *general transfer balance cap for the year -- nil."
GIVEN `concessional contributions cap` IS A NUMBER, `total superannuation balance` IS A NUMBER, `general transfer balance cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-concessional contributions cap` MEANS
    IF `total superannuation balance` AT LEAST `general transfer balance cap` THEN 0
    ELSE 4 TIMES `concessional contributions cap`

§§ `292-102 -- downsizer contributions`

-- s 292-102(1): covered if "(a) ... made ... when you are aged 55 years or over"; (b) from the capital proceeds of disposing of an
-- ownership interest in a dwelling; (c) you or your spouse held it; (d) the gain or loss is "wholly or partially disregarded
-- under Subdivision 118-B"; (e) the 10-year condition in (2); (f) "located in *Australia, and is not a caravan, houseboat or
-- other mobile home"; (g) "made within 90 days, or such longer period as the Commissioner allows, after the time the change of
-- ownership occurs"; (h) you choose; (i) no earlier downsizer contribution from another dwelling.
-- (2)(a): "at all times during the 10 years ending just before the disposal" held by you, your spouse or former spouse.
-- (3): only to the extent it does not exceed the lesser of "(a) $300,000, less any other contribution that is already covered
-- ... in respect of you; and (b) the sum of the *capital proceeds" from the interest and any related spousal interest, less
-- other downsizer contributions from them for you or your spouse.
DECLARE Downsizer HAS
    `age when contributing` IS A NUMBER
    `main residence exemption applied at least partly` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years held by the couple before the disposal` IS A NUMBER
    `dwelling in Australia and not mobile` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the change of ownership` IS A NUMBER
    `chosen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `earlier downsizer from another dwelling` IS A BOOLEAN
    `amount contributed` IS A NUMBER
    `your earlier downsizer contributions` IS A NUMBER
    `capital proceeds of both interests` IS A NUMBER
    `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Downsizer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contribution qualifies as a downsizer contribution` IF
        `the contribution`'s `age when contributing` AT LEAST 55
    AND `the contribution`'s `main residence exemption applied at least partly`
    AND `the contribution`'s `years held by the couple before the disposal` AT LEAST 10
    AND `the contribution`'s `dwelling in Australia and not mobile`
    AND `the contribution`'s `days after the change of ownership` AT MOST 90
    AND `the contribution`'s `chosen`
    AND (NOT `the contribution`'s `earlier downsizer from another dwelling`)

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Downsizer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the downsizer ceiling` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (300000 MINUS `the contribution`'s `your earlier downsizer contributions`) (`the contribution`'s `capital proceeds of both interests` MINUS `the contribution`'s `other downsizer contributions from these proceeds`)

GIVEN `the contribution` IS A Downsizer
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount covered as a downsizer contribution` MEANS
    IF `the contribution qualifies as a downsizer contribution` `the contribution`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the contribution`'s `amount contributed`) (`the downsizer ceiling` `the contribution`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `294-30, 294-35 -- transfer balance cap`

-- s 294-35(3): "The general transfer balance cap is: (a) for the 2017-2018 *financial year -- $1,600,000; or (b) for the
-- 2018-2019 financial year or a later financial year -- the amount worked out by indexing annually" (an INPUT for later years).
-- (1): your cap for the year you first have a transfer balance account equals the general cap for that year.
-- s 294-30(1): "You have excess transfer balance at a particular time if, at that time, the *transfer balance in your *transfer
-- balance account exceeds your *transfer balance cap"; (2) the transfer balance is credits less debits.
GIVEN `first financial year starting` IS A NUMBER, `indexed general cap for that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the transfer balance cap on first having an account` MEANS
    IF `first financial year starting` EQUALS 2017 THEN 1600000 ELSE `indexed general cap for that year`

GIVEN `credits` IS A NUMBER, `debits` IS A NUMBER, `transfer balance cap` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess transfer balance` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`credits` MINUS `debits` MINUS `transfer balance cap`) 0

§§ `301-10, 301-15 -- member benefits`

-- s 301-10: "If you are 60 years or over when you receive a *superannuation benefit, the benefit is not assessable income and is
-- not *exempt income." (Note 2: an element untaxed in the fund -- Subdiv 301-C, not encoded.)
-- s 301-15: under 60 but at preservation age, "the *tax free component of the benefit is not assessable income". Below 60 the
-- taxable component is assessable (ss 301-20, 301-25, 301-35, 301-40), with offsets not encoded; s 301-30 makes the tax free
-- component non-assessable below preservation age too, so preservation age does not change the assessable amount here.
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `taxable component` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessable part of a member benefit from a taxed fund` MEANS
    IF `age` AT LEAST 60 THEN 0
    ELSE `taxable component`

§§ `302-60, 302-140, 302-145, 302-195 -- death benefits`

-- s 302-195(1): "A death benefits dependant, of a person who has died, is: (a) the deceased person's *spouse or former spouse; or
-- (b) the deceased person's *child, aged less than 18; or (c) any other person with whom the deceased person had an
-- interdependency relationship under section 302-200 just before he or she died; or (d) any other person who was a dependant of
-- the deceased person just before he or she died."
-- s 302-60: "A *superannuation lump sum that you receive because of the death of a person of whom you are a *death benefits
-- dependant is not assessable income and is not *exempt income."
-- s 302-140: for a non-dependant, "The *tax free component ... is not assessable income"; s 302-145(1) "the *taxable component of
-- the lump sum is assessable income"; (2) an offset ensures "the rate of income tax on the *element taxed in the fund ... does not
-- exceed 15%"; (3) on the element untaxed in the fund, 30%.
DECLARE Recipient IS ONE OF
    `the spouse or former spouse`
    `a child under 18`
    `an adult child`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `recipient` IS A Recipient, `interdependent or dependent just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the recipient is a death benefits dependant` IF
    CONSIDER `recipient`
    WHEN `the spouse or former spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a child under 18` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `interdependent or dependent just before the death`

GIVEN `recipient` IS A Recipient, `interdependent or dependent just before the death` IS A BOOLEAN, `taxable component` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assessable part of a death benefit lump sum` MEANS
    IF `the recipient is a death benefits dependant` `recipient` `interdependent or dependent just before the death`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `taxable component`

-- The ceiling s 302-145(2) puts on the tax rate on the element taxed in the fund (15) or untaxed in the fund (30), in percent.
GIVEN `element untaxed in the fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum rate on a non-dependant's taxable component in percent` MEANS
    IF `element untaxed in the fund` THEN 30 ELSE 15
